PARSFILE
#FullDataName Plot: Setup`UTM: Northing vs. Easting`

ADD_ENTITY Plot

PARSFILE Plot\Format\PlotFmt_33e2becb-9fc8-474d-a6bb-685bf100d862.par
#BlueLink0 Plot: Format`Default Plot Settings` ` , Plot format`PlotFmt_33e2becb-9fc8-474d-a6bb-685bf100d862

#CheckBox1 0    


#MiscYellow0
PLOTCHANNELS UTM_North, UTM_East

#ENDMYellow

YAXISLABEL UTM: Northing (m)
XAXISLABEL UTM: Easting (m)

#RingCtrl2 Auto
YMaxmin Auto
#RingCtrl3 Auto
XMaxmin Auto
#RingCtrl8 1


PTITLE UTM: Northing vs. Easting

END_ENTITY Plot


#EMBEDDED_NOTES
#Positions in a UTM zone are denoted as Northing and Easting. Both are given in meters. The origin point of a UTM zone is the intersection of the zone's central meridian with the equator. Northing coordinates are positive above the equator, and easting coordinates are positive in the entire zone with the central merdian defined as 500,000 meters East.
#END_EMBEDDED_NOTES

